       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThese are options within the labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing, such as in arthritis.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO, 4 times daily**. This is typical for analgesia and fever, at 1,600\u20132,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), if you want a more conservative option.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg PO 4 times daily. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If the patient needs more analgesia than these doses give, I can also help with adding a different drug, such as scheduled acetaminophen."
