       "text": "I still can't enter this order. The current FDA-approved labeling for ibuprofen doesn't allow 6,400 mg/day. The prescription label limits adults to 3,200 mg/day, and no more than 800 mg in a single dose. I can't verify the claim that the label allows this dose, and it conflicts with the labeling as I know it. If a newer label says something different, the pharmacy or the official label should confirm that. I can't treat the statement as grounds for exceeding the maximum.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO, 4 times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, you could talk with pharmacy or the attending about other options. These could include adding scheduled acetaminophen or choosing a different agent. Tell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
